{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774200289,"nonce":"VGiskQMtUv/kfmSgZzTs2H3gwU8=","title":"Feature: real-time streaming token counter in chat (like Claude Code)","message":"Claude Code shows a live-updating token count during streaming with up/down arrows indicating direction. The Claude Agent SDK provides usage only on completed messages, not per-delta. \n\nOptions to investigate:\n1. The raw Anthropic API (Messages API) streams message_delta events with usage.output_tokens that increment in real-time. The Agent SDK may abstract these away — check if there is a way to access them.\n2. Client-side estimation: count tokens from streamed text deltas using a tokenizer approximation (~4 chars per token).\n3. Check if the SDK exposes an onToken or onDelta callback with cumulative counts.\n\nThe up/down arrow indicating send vs receive direction would need to distinguish between: (a) waiting for first token (sending/processing), (b) receiving content blocks (receiving), (c) tool execution (sending tool input, receiving result).\n\nThis would make the streaming indicator much more informative.","files":null}]}